--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -46,6 +46,16 @@
 
 Use a new or empty output directory. `--smoke` reduces dataset statistics for execution checks. `--categorical-events`, `--continuous-events` and `--pair-events` override the three event-count groups. Reduced statistics may skip representation checks for sparsely occupied bins; a smoke run is not a validated production dataset.
 
+Generation counts apply separately at each photon energy in each dataset split:
+
+| Setting | What the count applies to |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--categorical-events` | Each of process selection and shell selection at each photon energy |
+| `--continuous-events` | Each of Rayleigh and Compton at each photon energy; photoelectric sampling at each photon energy and shell |
+| `--pair-events` | Pair production at each photon energy above threshold |
+
+For example, `--continuous-events 8192` generates 8,192 Rayleigh events, 8,192 Compton events and 8,192 photoelectric events for each of the five shells at every selected photon energy. These are separate sample counts, not a combined total. The menu and command help spell out these inputs instead of calling them a "condition."
+
 ```bash
 python -m beamweaver train runs/data/schema_v4_data.npz --resume runs/training
 python -m beamweaver train runs/data/schema_v4_data.npz --resume runs/training --factor comp_u
